# Force LF line endings for text files, regardless of the checking-out
# machine's own git core.autocrlf setting. .gitattributes wins over that
# per-machine setting for any path it matches.
#
# Why this exists: this repo's provisioning pipeline spans Windows (the
# PowerShell ISO-writing tool used to build the classroom USB) and
# Linux/WSL2 (the 11e client, the server dev box). A Windows checkout with
# the common Git-for-Windows default core.autocrlf=true silently converts
# every text file to CRLF on checkout, with zero visible symptom until
# something actually executes the result.
#
# Found 2026-08-08: a CRLF-corrupted scripts/install.sh, staged onto a
# provisioning ISO by that Windows tooling, broke on its own
# `set -euo pipefail` (line 2) during a real preseed late_command run —
# `set` read the option as "pipefail<CR>", rejected it as invalid, and
# bash terminated the whole non-interactive script immediately with status
# 2 (the "failed with exit code 2" red screen). Every other line in the
# file carried the same trailing-CR-glued-to-last-token corruption, so this
# wasn't a one-line fix — see CLAUDE.md's Provisioning / Imaging section.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touched by line-ending normalization, listed
# explicitly so `text=auto`'s own binary detection isn't the only thing
# standing between these and corruption.
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.zip binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
